5. Jurisdiction-aware routing
Area	Local office	Escalation
Village	Gram Panchayat (Pradhan)	SDM office
Basti / urban	Ward head, then Nagar Nigam	SDM office for verification
Block and district	Block and District offices	State

Routing is rule-based on asset location and type, so each alert reaches the office that owns the fix.

6. Scalability path
Phase	Scope	Architecture change
1	One village, simulated data	Browser prototype (this repo)
2	Pilot village, real sensors	Add ESP32 nodes, LoRa gateway, FastAPI and database
3	Multiple Panchayats, district	Multi-tenant database, district dashboard, GIS integration
4	District and state	Government system integration, large-scale predictive analytics

The twin, the data flow and the work-order loop stay the same at every phase. Only the data source and storage change.

7. Design principles
Predict, don't just monitor: forecasts and compound-risk alerts come before failure.
One integrated view: water, roads and sanitation in a single twin.
Low cost: cheap sensors where they work, cameras where they don't.
Close the loop: every alert ends in a verified, logged fix.
Inclusive access: citizen reporting in Hindi or English, SMS for villagers without smartphones.
Graceful failure: a dead sensor or camera is itself an alert.
